      "internal": false,
      "mergeID": "60593ed9826873531caef366",
      "mergedPostDetails": "It's great to have this much more control over our eye tracking. It's also great that we have much more control over our visemes.\nBut, seeing what we've been given to create working visemes, I think it'd be more than just a matter of consistency to allow more options for eye tracking.\nSometimes bone rotations are not an option or wouldn't be the most optimal way of achieving eye tracking for some models. Not only that, but imagine the possibilities that would open up with new options should the Dev team decide to implement support for actual eye tracking.\nTL;DR More options for eye tracking. Some public float parameters would cover pretty much everything, but blendshapes may be a good start too.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "Public Eye Look parameters or Blend Shapes for eye tracking",
      "pinned": false,
      "postID": "5d984713b525c85b102e0cb3",
      "private": false,
      "spam": false,
      "synthetic": true,
      "value": ""
    },
